{
  "$comment": "Melogold sync scenarios: listening history (DESIGN §3.7, §3.11, §3.16; API §4.8). Each scenario starts with a fresh account whose devices are named in `devices`. A step sets the server clock to `now` and sends `ops` from `device` in one POST /sync; `results` are the expected OpResult fields in the order of `ops` (fields not listed are not compared; seq is for debugging only). After the last step, `expect` is the history stream of a pull from cursor \"\": `plays`, `playStats` and `playForgets` compared as sets (sorted here by eventId / videoId), with `device` naming the device whose deviceId the PlayRow carries. Times are API §1.5 strings.",
  "license": "CC0-1.0",
  "format": 1,
  "scenarios": [
    {
      "name": "clear-vs-offline-plays",
      "design": "DESIGN §3.16: A cleared the history at 12:00, B listened offline at 11:30 and 12:30 → only 12:30 stays in the history, the total counts both",
      "devices": ["phone", "laptop"],
      "steps": [
        {
          "now": "2026-09-23T11:05:00.000Z",
          "device": "phone",
          "ops": [
            {"opId": "e1000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001", "kind": "play.add", "at": "2026-09-23T11:00:00.000Z", "videoId": "a1B2c3D4e5F", "playedAt": "2026-09-23T11:00:00.000Z", "playTimeMs": 200000, "history": true, "playtime": true}
          ],
          "results": [{"status": "applied", "code": null, "replayed": false}]
        },
        {
          "now": "2026-09-23T12:00:00.000Z",
